==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Monk Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Sanzo Cat''' at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bishop Cat lacks both the stats to be a usable fighter and the range to have an impact on any early-game [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy, as they all outrange it in the first place. While Bishop Cat can be of use against certain event or collaboration event enemies, it is, in general, best to avoid using Bishop Cat outside of its True Form.

When used against Floating enemies it does outrange, this unit is best spammed, ideally in conjunction with another [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] staller like [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] to increase uptime.

==='''True Form'''===
Thanks to its additional 50 range and Area Attack, Sanzo Cat can now make proper use of a very effective Slow ability. His range may only be 250, but that is more than enough to take care of most melee Floating enemies such as the [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]] [[Teacher Bun Bun#Variants|variants]] and the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s. He remains ineffective against most Floating enemies with longer range than him, but fortunately, they tend to attack slowly and don't need much stalling in the first place, allowing him to steamroll most Floating-dominant stages in the early to midgame.

This unit can become a nearly impassable wall against the aforementioned Bun Bun and Cyclone variants, making it vital to create an opportunity for a stack to form. For this reason, Sanzo Cat is best used with "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] or very tanky units, as well as (ideally [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]) units who can take care of other traits.

However, as players progress further, Sanzo's value drops significantly. 250 range simply isn't enough to keep such a fragile unit away from the line of fire, which prevents them from even forming a stack in the first place outside of very specific circumstances. Meanwhile, [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] continue to remain effective as anti-Floating specialists due to their stat-based abilities giving them greater survivability and consistency.

==='''Talents'''===
Sanzo Cat's most important Talent is Target [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]. Despite falling off later on (primarily to the existence of [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom]] and even [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble]], both of which seek to overwhelm Angels through sheer DPS instead), this is still a worthwhile investment due to the prevalence of notorious melee angels such as [[Boraphim]], [[Divine Cyclone]] and [[St. Dober]], or even just [[Angelic Gory]]. Against Angels, Talented Sanzo easily supersedes [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Catophone]], as its sheer disposability and attack speed can partially compensate its own range disadvantage and activation chance. Combined with the likes of Ramen, Sanzo can gravely cripple these nasty melee Angels. Sanzo even has an edge against [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]], whose higher range, superior activation chance and fast attack rate are offset by Single Attack and an expensive unlock requirement, to the point where Sanzo would certainly be relied upon before he becomes available.

His [[Weaken]] Talent can be combined with the original Slow ability to have better control on the battlefield and increase the ease of stacking many Sanzo Cats. Only the first level is necessary, but it may be worthwhile to upgrade it fully as well, however, the weaken reduces attack to 70%, meaning that pairing it with units such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can be more detrimental as the less effective weaken can override the stronger one, though if you don't rely on the weaken as much, you can consider getting it. The other Talents all further contribute to making Sanzo Cats last longer on the battlefield as well as needing less of them to permanently slow foes, making all Talents worth considering, minus Defense Buff if Sanzo Cat's level is too low for increased health to make a difference. Either way, Target Angel and Weaken should be given top priority over the rest.

==='''Orb'''===
Defence Up against Angels is arguably the best option for Effect Orbs, due to how easily [[Gabriel]]s slip past defences, followed closely by Defence Up against Floating. Nothing else is worth considering. Either way, the effect is usually minuscule, so there's no need to dedicate any in the first place.

Death Mini-Surge may provide some form of stack insurance, potentially slowing and weakening hordes of Floating and Angel enemies, though Cash Back is more direct, lessening the blow to your cash reserves.

