==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Bishop Cat's slow chance from 10% to 20%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Bishop Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Bustin' Ghosts (Removed Combo)|Bustin' Ghosts]] and [[Dharma (Removed Combo)|Dharma]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Bishop Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Bishop Cat
A merciful Cat that brings peace and love
to all of its followers. Charges for confessions.
Might slow Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Monk Cat
Envelopes the enemies in gracious serenity
to allow them to move to the afterlife
Might slow Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Sanzo Cat
On a journey to save souls through enlightenment.
Mostly just beats up the local wildlife, though.
Might slow Floating enemies (Area Attack)</pre>
*Bishop Cat appears to have been modeled after the [[wikia:dragonquest:Priest|Priests]] from ''[[wikia:dragonquest:Dragon Quest III|Dragon Quest III]]''.
*Sanzo Cat is based on the ''[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]'' character [[wikipedia:Tang Sanzang|Tang Sanzang]], a Buddhist monk whose Japanese name is Genjo Sanzō.
**The monkey Sanzo Cat has with them is likely a reference to [[wikipedia:Sun Wukong|Sun Wukong]], who is also known as the Monkey King.
*Monk Cat appears to be carrying a [[wikipedia:Wooden fish|wooden fish]] alongside its padded staff.

